hi this is presh talwalkar  in this video i'm going to teach you a  really cool mental math trick of how you  can multiply any two numbers that end in  the digit five  i'll explain this process with several  examples and then i'll show you how you  can use it to solve many related  mathematical problems  at the end of the video i'll give you a  proof of why this method works  let's say you want to multiply 15 by 35  both the numbers 15 and 35  have a last digit of five  so there's a quick way we can solve this  the steps are to add the product and  average of the leading digits of the  number  we multiply that result by a hundred  and then we add 25  so let me go over these steps in detail  the numbers 15 and 35 both end in the  digit 5.  for the rest of the calculation we can  ignore these digits of 5 and focus on  just the leading digits of the number  the first step is to add the product and  the average of these digits  we find the product by multiplying one  by three to get three and we find the  average by taking the average of one and  three which is two  so we add the product of three to the  average of two to get five  and that's the hard part of the  computation the rest of it will be easy  we multiply this by a hundred to get  five hundred  and finally we add twenty five  we get the result of five hundred and  twenty five  and that's our answer fifteen times  thirty five is five hundred and twenty  five  let's do another example of this  technique  let's say you want to multiply 65 by 75  both of these numbers end in the digit 5  so we can cover up the digit 5.  we now want to multiply these digits to  get 42 and we take the average which is  6.5  adding this together we get 48.5  now we multiply by 100 to get 48.50  and then we add 25.  so we have 48.75  and that's our answer 65 by 75 is 48.75  you can also do this for digits for  numbers which have more than two digits  let's say you want to do 35 by a hundred  and fifteen  both of these numbers end in the digit  five  so we cover up the five and we only need  to do calculation for the leading digits  the product of three and eleven is  thirty three  the average of three and eleven is seven  adding these together we get forty  we then multiply by a hundred and  finally we add twenty five  this gets a result of four thousand  twenty five and that's the answer of  thirty five times a hundred and fifteen  so you can actually use this technique  to solve other problems let's say you  wanted to fill 14 gallons of gas at 3.18  cents  that would be the problem 14 times 3.18  now you can't use the technique because  neither of these numbers end in five  but you can estimate by considering a  related problem  what if you wanted to fill 15 gallons at  315 cents per gallon  that would be the problem of 15 times  315  so now both of these numbers end in the  digit 5 so we can use the technique that  we just learned in this video  we cover up the 5  then we take the product of 1 and 31  which is 31  we take the average which is 16  we add these together  and then we multiply by a hundred and  add 25.  so we get that 15 times 315 is  47.25  if we convert this back into dollars we  get 15 times 3.15 is 47.25  now we only wanted to fit this is to  estimate filling 15 gallons but of  course we only need to fill 14 gallons  so if we wanted to fill one fewer gallon  we would be multiplying 14 by 315.  so we subtract 315 from 47.25  so we subtract three dollars we get to  44 then we subtract 15 cents and then we  get 10 cents  so we figured out that 14 times 315 is  4410  and this is extraordinarily close  we wanted to solve 14 by 318  and that's 4452.  so using this process of multiplying two  numbers ending in five and doing a  slight modification we actually were  able to get within 42 cents of the exact  answer and we could do this all in our  head  so why does this technique work  if you're multiplying two numbers that  end in five that's multiplying the  binomials 10x plus five times 10y plus  five the x and y are the leading digits  of the number  if we expand this out we get a hundred  xy plus fifty times x plus y plus twenty  five  now fifty is one half of a hundred  so we can factor out a hundred and then  we get a hundred xy  plus the average of x plus y  and finally we add on 25 at the end  and this is the formula we've been using  in this video  x y is the product  x plus y over two is the average  so this is adding the product and  average of the leading digits  we're then multiplying by a hundred  that's the hundred part and then finally  we're adding 25.  if you like this video please check out  my book the best mental math trick  it includes techniques like this  complete with applications and examples  and mathematical proofs of why they work  there's a link in the video description  thanks for watching please subscribe to  my channel  you can catch me on my blog mind your  decisions which you can follow on  facebook google plus and patreon  you can also catch me on social media at  preshtalwalker  and you can check out all my books there  are descriptions in the video  description

